nodecode-minimizer is a rewrite of nosliwhtes's nosliwhtes/hermes-minimizer:
https://github.com/nosliwhtes/hermes-minimizer
commit d209ed0824e2787cd6454bd4b060dbf0381b7b79
MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Seth Wilson (LICENSE)

The original is one static section of Hermes's system prompt, registered at
plugin load and never changed: a Python file that read a bundled policy.md and
handed its text to the runtime. Nothing of that shape survives here, because
Nodecode has no section a folder may append to the system prompt. What was
rewritten is the carrier and the surface: the same policy.md text, whole and
unchanged, rides the :ROUND point so it lands in the first request of every
turn; a /minimizer command and a (help :minimizer) topic read it back, with a
max_chars cap and a brief mode that carries the rung ladder alone, neither of
which the original offered. What was left out is Hermes's own manifest, its
register() call and its doctor gate, which have no meaning in an image that
loads a folder by its presence; no tool, hook or dependency of the original
was dropped, since it had none. Nothing is enforced here either, exactly as
before: the policy advises, and says in its own first line that system, user
and repository instructions outrank it.
